1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:02,120
Why does a knee
replacement still hurt

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,107
when the X-ray says it
looks fine?

3
00:00:04,408 --> 00:00:04,911
Let me show

4
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:06,237
you on this knee model.

5
00:00:06,594 --> 00:00:07,728
As you can see,

6
00:00:07,728 --> 00:00:08,686
a new knee is made

7
00:00:08,686 --> 00:00:09,514
of a metal piece

8
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:10,779
on the thigh bone,

9
00:00:10,779 --> 00:00:12,667
a metal piece on the shin
bone,

10
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:14,710
and a plastic spacer in
between.

11
00:00:14,955 --> 00:00:17,336
Now, the part nobody shows
you

12
00:00:17,336 --> 00:00:18,867
is what's wrapped around
it.

13
00:00:19,038 --> 00:00:20,516
It's living tissue,

14
00:00:20,516 --> 00:00:21,688
and it surrounds the whole

15
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,117
joint like a sleeve.

16
00:00:23,371 --> 00:00:25,343
This tissue has to bend
and stretch

17
00:00:25,343 --> 00:00:27,414
every single time your
knee moves.

18
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:28,738
Now, to put the new

19
00:00:28,738 --> 00:00:30,272
joint in, the surgeon has

20
00:00:30,272 --> 00:00:32,114
to work through that
living tissue,

21
00:00:32,114 --> 00:00:34,361
and afterward it gets
inflamed and swollen.

22
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:36,687
At first, that's
completely normal.

23
00:00:36,727 --> 00:00:37,870
But in some people,

24
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:39,172
the swelling hangs on much

25
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:40,918
longer than anyone
expects.

26
00:00:41,051 --> 00:00:42,948
Now there's more swollen
tissue sitting

27
00:00:42,948 --> 00:00:44,529
in the same small space,

28
00:00:44,529 --> 00:00:45,525
and you see this room

29
00:00:45,525 --> 00:00:46,591
around the joint?

30
00:00:46,789 --> 00:00:48,609
That's what a calm knee
looks like.

31
00:00:48,705 --> 00:00:49,700
But many of us,

32
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,133
through no fault of our
own,

33
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:52,376
don't have that room.

34
00:00:52,602 --> 00:00:55,262
Instead, the swollen
tissue crowds in

35
00:00:55,262 --> 00:00:56,573
around the new joint,

36
00:00:56,573 --> 00:00:58,219
and every time you bend,

37
00:00:58,219 --> 00:00:59,707
it gets compressed,

38
00:00:59,707 --> 00:01:01,270
and every time you
straighten,

39
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,345
it gets stretched.

40
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,134
This is what's causing
that tight

41
00:01:04,134 --> 00:01:05,604
band around your knee,

42
00:01:05,604 --> 00:01:07,427
that deep ache on the
stairs,

43
00:01:07,427 --> 00:01:08,803
and that throbbing that
wakes

44
00:01:08,803 --> 00:01:09,804
you up at night.

45
00:01:09,965 --> 00:01:12,551
We call that The Squeeze,

46
00:01:12,551 --> 00:01:14,318
and it can be behind the
stiffness,

47
00:01:14,318 --> 00:01:15,518
the pressure,

48
00:01:15,518 --> 00:01:16,913
the ache when you stand
up,

49
00:01:16,913 --> 00:01:17,610
and even the ache

50
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:18,946
when you're sitting still.

51
00:01:19,117 --> 00:01:20,624
If that sounds confusing,

52
00:01:20,624 --> 00:01:22,201
I'm sorry, but don't
worry.

53
00:01:22,409 --> 00:01:23,962
Here's the secret not many

54
00:01:23,962 --> 00:01:25,236
people know about,

55
00:01:25,236 --> 00:01:26,703
but everyone should know.

56
00:01:26,827 --> 00:01:29,273
Your replacement can be
perfectly fine,

57
00:01:29,273 --> 00:01:31,430
while the swollen tissue
around it

58
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:33,114
makes your knee feel like
something

59
00:01:33,114 --> 00:01:35,281
is squeezing it from the
inside,

60
00:01:35,281 --> 00:01:37,038
and the more swollen it
is,

61
00:01:37,038 --> 00:01:38,533
the tighter it feels.

62
00:01:38,573 --> 00:01:40,256
But that's only half of
the answer,

63
00:01:40,256 --> 00:01:40,647
you see,

64
00:01:40,647 --> 00:01:43,400
because an X-ray shows
metal and bone,

65
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,787
and it can't show swollen
soft tissue.

66
00:01:45,827 --> 00:01:47,306
So when they tell you
"everything

67
00:01:47,306 --> 00:01:48,924
looks good," they're
right,

68
00:01:48,924 --> 00:01:50,186
about the implant.

69
00:01:50,384 --> 00:01:52,886
So since 2014,

70
00:01:52,886 --> 00:01:54,234
when my wife had her own

71
00:01:54,234 --> 00:01:55,871
knee replaced and kept
hurting

72
00:01:55,871 --> 00:01:58,466
long after the X-rays
looked fine,

73
00:01:58,466 --> 00:02:00,084
I've been researching
everything there

74
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:01,107
is to know about pain

75
00:02:01,107 --> 00:02:02,453
after a knee replacement.

76
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,716
I've dedicated my career
as a physical

77
00:02:04,716 --> 00:02:06,260
therapist to helping
people like

78
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,552
her, because I've seen how

79
00:02:07,552 --> 00:02:08,947
it makes you literally

80
00:02:08,947 --> 00:02:10,628
a prisoner of your own
body.

81
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:12,571
What I found was shocking.

82
00:02:12,695 --> 00:02:13,923
The crazy part,

83
00:02:13,923 --> 00:02:15,482
no one is talking about
it.

84
00:02:15,653 --> 00:02:17,941
That's because once the
X-ray looks good,

85
00:02:17,941 --> 00:02:20,486
the conversation usually
stops.

86
00:02:20,787 --> 00:02:22,563
About 1 in 5 people still

87
00:02:22,563 --> 00:02:24,367
hurt after a knee
replacement,

88
00:02:24,367 --> 00:02:25,474
and many of them are sent

89
00:02:25,474 --> 00:02:27,111
home with pain pills and
told

90
00:02:27,111 --> 00:02:28,112
to give it time.

91
00:02:28,292 --> 00:02:30,589
Unfortunately, a good
X-ray becomes

92
00:02:30,589 --> 00:02:32,446
the answer to a pain
question.

93
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,337
But one day I came across

94
00:02:34,337 --> 00:02:36,104
something that can change
lives,

95
00:02:36,104 --> 00:02:37,663
and it can change yours
too.

96
00:02:37,815 --> 00:02:38,624
You see,

97
00:02:38,624 --> 00:02:39,936
deep in the tissue around

98
00:02:39,936 --> 00:02:40,959
your new knee

99
00:02:40,959 --> 00:02:43,274
is something called
inflammation,

100
00:02:43,274 --> 00:02:45,209
and this alarm signal is
the real

101
00:02:45,209 --> 00:02:47,345
culprit behind The
Squeeze.

102
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,143
For such a small signal,

103
00:02:49,143 --> 00:02:51,483
it causes a huge number of
problems.

104
00:02:51,589 --> 00:02:53,040
Did you know you may not
even

105
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,627
see the swelling from the
outside?

106
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:55,774
That's because a lot

107
00:02:55,774 --> 00:02:56,936
of it sits deep,

108
00:02:56,936 --> 00:02:58,031
around the joint.

109
00:02:58,146 --> 00:02:59,550
Odds are you've looked
down

110
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:00,638
at your knee and thought,

111
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:02,507
"It doesn't even look that
swollen,"

112
00:03:02,507 --> 00:03:04,135
and yet it still feels
tight,

113
00:03:04,135 --> 00:03:06,178
especially after a day on
your feet.

114
00:03:06,302 --> 00:03:07,157
Now, if you're asking

115
00:03:07,157 --> 00:03:09,017
the logical next question,

116
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:10,310
how do I calm the swollen

117
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:12,000
tissue around my new knee?

118
00:03:12,338 --> 00:03:13,097
Good job.

119
00:03:13,137 --> 00:03:14,752
You're asking the right
question.

120
00:03:14,932 --> 00:03:15,239
You see,

121
00:03:15,239 --> 00:03:16,960
what I'm sharing with you
today took

122
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,690
over a decade to learn,

123
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:20,029
but despite all those
years

124
00:03:20,029 --> 00:03:21,489
studying the real cause,

125
00:03:21,489 --> 00:03:23,634
there was no simple
solution in sight.

126
00:03:23,842 --> 00:03:25,699
My wife was losing hope.

127
00:03:25,739 --> 00:03:27,931
She thought maybe there's
really no answer.

128
00:03:28,074 --> 00:03:29,329
Maybe it's something she'd
just

129
00:03:29,329 --> 00:03:30,377
have to live with.

130
00:03:30,464 --> 00:03:32,079
Boy, were we wrong.

131
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:33,086
One day,

132
00:03:33,086 --> 00:03:35,551
I came across a small
company called

133
00:03:35,551 --> 00:03:36,738
KenRelief.

134
00:03:36,834 --> 00:03:40,210
They specialize in at-home
wraps that use

135
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:42,821
red and near-infrared
light.

136
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:44,423
I read through the
research

137
00:03:44,423 --> 00:03:46,255
they'd gathered on the
technology,

138
00:03:46,255 --> 00:03:47,911
and let me tell you, after
reading

139
00:03:47,911 --> 00:03:49,991
it, I knew this was the
answer.

140
00:03:50,152 --> 00:03:51,656
I was excited.

141
00:03:51,808 --> 00:03:54,105
I immediately contacted
their customer service

142
00:03:54,105 --> 00:03:55,100
and asked them to connect

143
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:56,244
me with the founders,

144
00:03:56,244 --> 00:03:58,575
because I had something
important to discuss.

145
00:03:58,727 --> 00:03:59,583
An hour later,

146
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:00,345
I was on a phone

147
00:04:00,345 --> 00:04:01,681
call with the founders.

148
00:04:01,787 --> 00:04:03,684
I shared my background
with them,

149
00:04:03,684 --> 00:04:04,354
and after a bit

150
00:04:04,354 --> 00:04:05,488
of back and forth,

151
00:04:05,488 --> 00:04:07,460
they invited me to their
headquarters,

152
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,567
and soon after,

153
00:04:08,567 --> 00:04:09,952
we were working together,

154
00:04:09,952 --> 00:04:12,175
because they needed a
physical therapist

155
00:04:12,175 --> 00:04:14,004
who knew replacement
patients.

156
00:04:14,082 --> 00:04:15,533
Many months and more
prototypes

157
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:16,769
than I can count later,

158
00:04:16,769 --> 00:04:17,755
we finally had a wrap

159
00:04:17,755 --> 00:04:18,899
that targets the swollen,

160
00:04:18,899 --> 00:04:21,159
irritated tissue around
the new joint,

161
00:04:21,159 --> 00:04:22,554
using light, without heat,

162
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:23,624
without pressure,

163
00:04:23,624 --> 00:04:25,183
and without touching the
implant.

164
00:04:25,326 --> 00:04:27,056
It's called the KenRelief
Red

165
00:04:27,056 --> 00:04:28,451
Light Therapy Wrap,

166
00:04:28,451 --> 00:04:31,256
and it uses FDA cleared
technology.

167
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:33,259
The secret is two
wavelengths

168
00:04:33,259 --> 00:04:34,440
working together:

169
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,644
660 nanometer red light

170
00:04:36,644 --> 00:04:39,580
and 850 nanometer
near-infrared light.

171
00:04:39,862 --> 00:04:42,085
Red and near-infrared
light has been studied

172
00:04:42,085 --> 00:04:44,252
for its ability to calm
inflammation,

173
00:04:44,252 --> 00:04:45,647
which may help the
irritated

174
00:04:45,647 --> 00:04:47,525
tissue take up less room,

175
00:04:47,525 --> 00:04:48,520
and that can mean less

176
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,359
pressure squeezing the new
joint.

177
00:04:50,501 --> 00:04:52,817
The near-infrared light
reaches deeper,

178
00:04:52,817 --> 00:04:54,463
into the tissue around the
joint that's

179
00:04:54,463 --> 00:04:56,072
been causing that constant
tight,

180
00:04:56,072 --> 00:04:57,383
squeezed feeling,

181
00:04:57,383 --> 00:04:59,259
making you nervous about
every step.

182
00:04:59,355 --> 00:05:00,164
You see,

183
00:05:00,164 --> 00:05:01,885
when that tissue calms
down,

184
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:03,317
there's less squeezing:

185
00:05:03,317 --> 00:05:04,945
less pressure when you
bend,

186
00:05:04,945 --> 00:05:06,727
and less tension when you
straighten.

187
00:05:06,767 --> 00:05:08,358
This can make it easier

188
00:05:08,358 --> 00:05:09,595
to get up from the couch,

189
00:05:09,595 --> 00:05:10,673
take the stairs,

190
00:05:10,673 --> 00:05:11,659
and who knows,

191
00:05:11,659 --> 00:05:12,710
maybe even get back out

192
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:13,525
in the garden.

193
00:05:13,724 --> 00:05:14,728
The best part,

194
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:16,474
it's so simple to use.

195
00:05:16,654 --> 00:05:17,584
All you need to do

196
00:05:17,584 --> 00:05:18,904
is strap it on for 20

197
00:05:18,904 --> 00:05:20,383
to 30 minutes a day,

198
00:05:20,383 --> 00:05:21,955
sitting in your favorite
chair,

199
00:05:21,955 --> 00:05:23,722
and most people notice a
meaningful

200
00:05:23,722 --> 00:05:25,625
difference by weeks two to
four.

201
00:05:25,768 --> 00:05:27,135
What's more surprising

202
00:05:27,135 --> 00:05:28,986
is that it's not a quick
fix,

203
00:05:28,986 --> 00:05:30,126
and that's the point.

204
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,650
The relief you've had
before wore off;

205
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:34,572
this builds day by day.

206
00:05:34,659 --> 00:05:35,840
In a randomized trial,

207
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,700
patients who received
light therapy

208
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,746
after total knee
replacement

209
00:05:39,746 --> 00:05:41,392
had less pain and swelling

210
00:05:41,392 --> 00:05:42,840
than patients who didn't.

211
00:05:43,094 --> 00:05:45,168
Now, I'd like you to
imagine waking

212
00:05:45,168 --> 00:05:46,730
up in the morning and not

213
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:48,197
thinking about your knee
at all.

214
00:05:48,237 --> 00:05:48,894
Why?

215
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,311
Because a knee is best

216
00:05:50,311 --> 00:05:51,628
when you forget it's
there.

217
00:05:51,799 --> 00:05:53,259
No counting the stairs,

218
00:05:53,259 --> 00:05:55,277
no scanning the room for a
chair,

219
00:05:55,277 --> 00:05:56,858
no saying "you go ahead,

220
00:05:56,858 --> 00:05:58,895
I'll stay here," just
freedom,

221
00:05:58,895 --> 00:06:00,179
sleeping through the night
without

222
00:06:00,179 --> 00:06:01,918
that throbbing waking you
up,

223
00:06:01,918 --> 00:06:03,248
and your first thought in
the morning

224
00:06:03,248 --> 00:06:05,170
can be breakfast instead
of your knee.

225
00:06:05,396 --> 00:06:07,312
Imagine finally getting
control back over

226
00:06:07,312 --> 00:06:08,620
your life and your body.

227
00:06:08,781 --> 00:06:10,651
Again, doing all the
things

228
00:06:10,651 --> 00:06:12,241
you love with your loved
ones,

229
00:06:12,241 --> 00:06:14,082
that feeling is priceless,

230
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,356
and that's the kind of
result

231
00:06:15,356 --> 00:06:16,804
I want you to experience.

232
00:06:16,854 --> 00:06:18,999
Now, check out some of
these results.

233
00:06:19,095 --> 00:06:19,914
Here's Rick,

234
00:06:19,914 --> 00:06:21,550
who's been struggling with
his replaced

235
00:06:21,550 --> 00:06:22,983
knee for two years

236
00:06:22,983 --> 00:06:23,959
and was starting to hear

237
00:06:23,959 --> 00:06:25,565
the word "revision."

238
00:06:25,661 --> 00:06:26,759
My wife saw an ad

239
00:06:26,759 --> 00:06:28,330
for the KenRelief wrap,

240
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:29,474
and she wanted to avoid

241
00:06:29,474 --> 00:06:31,322
another surgery at all
costs.

242
00:06:31,613 --> 00:06:32,618
So after doing a little

243
00:06:32,618 --> 00:06:33,910
bit of research

244
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:35,919
and seeing all the
positive reviews,

245
00:06:35,919 --> 00:06:37,674
we decided to give it a
try.

246
00:06:37,714 --> 00:06:39,329
Now, take it from me.

247
00:06:39,537 --> 00:06:40,755
After about three weeks,

248
00:06:40,755 --> 00:06:42,085
the tight band around

249
00:06:42,085 --> 00:06:43,486
my knee started loosening.

250
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:44,801
To this day,

251
00:06:44,801 --> 00:06:45,824
it's the only thing that's

252
00:06:45,824 --> 00:06:47,052
made a real difference,

253
00:06:47,052 --> 00:06:48,769
and it gave me my mornings
back.

254
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:50,074
Now I can enjoy the things

255
00:06:50,074 --> 00:06:51,106
I used to love,

256
00:06:51,106 --> 00:06:52,381
like long walks,

257
00:06:52,381 --> 00:06:53,757
nine holes of golf,

258
00:06:53,757 --> 00:06:55,381
and evenings out with my
wife.

259
00:06:55,784 --> 00:06:56,684
Thank you, KenRelief.

260
00:06:56,724 --> 00:06:58,757
This is exactly what I
needed.

261
00:06:59,095 --> 00:07:00,221
And here's Kristen,

262
00:07:00,221 --> 00:07:02,564
who loves spending time
with her grandkids,

263
00:07:02,564 --> 00:07:03,466
but couldn't enjoy

264
00:07:03,466 --> 00:07:04,765
it because of her knee.

265
00:07:04,945 --> 00:07:07,341
Honestly, I was at rock
bottom.

266
00:07:08,126 --> 00:07:10,367
My knee had gotten so
stiff

267
00:07:10,367 --> 00:07:11,911
that I had to stop doing
all

268
00:07:11,911 --> 00:07:13,396
the things I love to do.

269
00:07:13,687 --> 00:07:15,721
I couldn't even kneel in
the garden.

270
00:07:16,003 --> 00:07:18,204
I had problems getting
into my car.

271
00:07:18,319 --> 00:07:18,784
I mean,

272
00:07:18,784 --> 00:07:20,291
I know I'm not 20 anymore,

273
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:21,999
but I'm not 90 either.

274
00:07:22,271 --> 00:07:23,756
I took the pain pills.

275
00:07:23,955 --> 00:07:25,694
They're fine for
short-term relief,

276
00:07:25,694 --> 00:07:27,805
but I'm already on enough
medication,

277
00:07:27,805 --> 00:07:29,336
and they upset my stomach.

